The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
avs_get_module_entry(adev, &AVS_PROBE_MOD_UUID, &mentry);
```
```c
avs_dsp_delete_module(adev, mentry.module_id, 0, INVALID_PIPELINE_ID, 0);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the return value of `avs_get_module_entry()` is not checked. If this function fails, it may lead to accessing an invalid `mentry` structure, which can cause undefined behavior or crashes when trying to use `mentry.module_id` in subsequent operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = avs_get_module_entry(adev, &AVS_PROBE_MOD_UUID, &mentry);
if (ret)
    return ret;
```
```c
ret = avs_get_module_entry(adev, &AVS_PROBE_MOD_UUID, &mentry);
if (!ret)
    avs_dsp_delete_module(adev, mentry.module_id, 0, INVALID_PIPELINE_ID, 0);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces error handling by checking the return value of `avs_get_module_entry()`. If the function fails (indicated by a non-zero return value), the function will return early, preventing any further operations that depend on a valid `mentry`. This ensures that the code does not attempt to access or manipulate an invalid module entry, thus avoiding potential crashes or undefined behavior.

